index 80665d66..e805f561 100644
--- a/docs/harness/log.md
+++ b/docs/harness/log.md
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@ One entry per significant change: date, what changed, what was learned, what is
 - **Dev dependency added.** `flake8` in `requirements-devel.in`; `requirements-devel.txt` regenerated with `pip-compile` without `--upgrade` (only additions: flake8, mccabe, pycodestyle, pyflakes).
 - **Secret in tracked code, not changed.** `settings/common.py:249` holds a hard-coded `SECRET_KEY`. See the TODO in `AGENTS.md` and the `blocked` list of the harness build.
 
+## 2026-11-02: project invitation tokens expire after one week
+
+- **What changed.** New setting `INVITATION_TOKEN_LIFETIME = timedelta(days=7)` in `settings/common.py` (the same period as project transfer tokens, which hard-code 7 days in `taiga/projects/services/transfer.py`). `taiga/projects/services/invitations.py` has `generate_invitation_token()` (returns token and expiration date), `set_invitation_token(membership)` and `valid_invitations_filter()`. All issuers use the helper: membership create (`MembershipViewSet.pre_save`), bulk create (`services/members.py`), project import (`export_import/services/store.py`) and `sample_data`. `get_membership_by_token` (login and private register) and `InvitationViewSet` (GET `/invitations/<token>`) only match tokens with `token_expires_at` in the future, so expired and legacy tokens (no expiration date) return 404. `resend_invitation` rotates the token and its expiration date. Factories set `token_expires_at` one week ahead. Tests: `tests/integration/test_invitation_token_expiration.py`.
+- **What we learned.** Other worktrees share the compose PostgreSQL and its `test_taiga` database. When another session uses it, pytest fails with "database is being accessed by other users". A settings module outside the repo that imports `tests.config` and sets `DATABASES["default"]["TEST"]["NAME"]` to a unique name, used with `--ds=... --create-db`, avoids the conflict.
+- **What is left.** Pending invitations already in production databases have no expiration date and stop working after deploy: admins must resend them. The front end may want a clearer message than 404 for an expired invitation.
+
 ## 2026-11-01: fast gate output shows the test run
 
 - **What changed.** `make test-unit` (used by `make check-fast`) ran `pytest tests/unit --reuse-db -q`. The `-q` flag hides the pytest header ("test session starts", "collected N items") and the file names, so the harness verifier reported that the fast gate ran no tests, although 238 tests passed. The target now runs `pytest tests/unit --reuse-db -rA --tb=short`: the output shows the header, one line per test file, one `PASSED <test id>` line per test and the final summary (`238 passed`). No test or check was removed.
